.TH GPS-STATION 8 "October 2026" "gps-station" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
gps-station \- GPS time for ntpsec and the grid square for an sBitx or zBitx
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gps-station
.RB [ \-\-radio
.IR host:port ]
.RB [ \-\-gpsd
.IR host:port ]
.RB [ \-\-chars " 4|6]"
.RB [ \-\-conf
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-conf\-dir
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-service
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-ntp ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-grid ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.br
.B gps-station \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gps-station
runs as a systemd service beside
.BR gpsd (8)
and does two jobs.
.PP
.B Time.
When gpsd starts writing time to shared memory, it writes a
.B refclock shm
line to
.IR /etc/ntpsec/conf.d/gps-station.conf ,
adds
.B includefile /etc/ntpsec/conf.d/
to the end of
.I /etc/ntpsec/ntp.conf
once, and restarts ntpsec.
The file also sets
.B tos minsane 1
so the GPS alone can set the clock without a network.
Later, while ntpd follows a network server and has heard the GPS for eight
polls, it measures how late the GPS's NMEA time arrives over ten polls,
sets that as
.BR time1 ,
marks the file calibrated and restarts ntpsec once more.
If ntp.conf or another file in conf.d already has a refclock shm line,
ntpsec is left alone.
gpsd must be started with
.B \-n
for its time to reach shared memory; if it isn't, this is logged.
.PP
.B Grid.
It works out the Maidenhead locator from the fix and, once it has held for
a minute, sets it on the radio over TCP: zbitxre with
.BR "MYGRID FN31pr" ,
sbitx with
.BR "grid FN31pr" .
It retries until the radio answers and the new grid reads back.
A grid typed on the radio is left alone until the GPS moves to another
square.
.PP
The time job needs root; the grid job alone does not.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-radio " host:port"
The radio software's TCP port (default 127.0.0.1:8081).
.TP
.BI \-\-gpsd " host:port"
gpsd (default 127.0.0.1:2947).
.TP
.BR \-\-chars " 4|6"
Send a 4- or 6-character grid (default 6).
.TP
.BI \-\-conf " path"
ntpsec's main configuration (default /etc/ntpsec/ntp.conf).
.TP
.BI \-\-conf\-dir " path"
The directory included from it, holding gps-station.conf
(default /etc/ntpsec/conf.d).
.TP
.BI \-\-service " name"
ntpsec's systemd unit (default ntpsec).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-ntp
Only set the grid.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-grid
Only look after ntpsec.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Change nothing; log what would be done.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/default/gps-station
Options for the service, in
.BR GPS_STATION_ARGS .
.TP
.I /etc/ntpsec/conf.d/gps-station.conf
The GPS refclock, its time1 and whether it has been calibrated.
To measure again, change
.B calibrated=yes
to
.B calibrated=no
and restart the service.
.TP
.I /etc/default/gpsd
Needs
.BR GPSD_OPTIONS="\-n" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gps-station-desktop (1),
.BR gpsd (8),
.BR ntpd (8),
.BR ntpq (1)
.PP
https://github.com/jchonig/bitx-gps-station
